      { id: "da_m10", question: "Why is a dual-axis chart with two divergent Y-axes often considered a misleading data visualization practice?", options: ["It uses too many colors", "Manipulating the scale, min, and max of the secondary axis can visually exaggerate or invent false correlations between unrelated variables", "Browsers cannot render dual axes", "It slows down dashboard rendering"], answer: 1, explanation: "Dual axes allow arbitrary scaling of independent metrics, visually fabricating misleading intersections and slopes." }
